<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tosora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tosora is a village in Wajo Regency, South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tempe">Lake Tempe</a>, that was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> kingdom of Wajo. It was the seat of the elected ruler, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-matoa">Arung Matoa</a>, and of Wajo's council of lords. In 1670, after Wajo had sided with Gowa in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makassar-war">Makassar War</a>, forces of Bone and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> captured the town.</p></div>
